Renoir inventory and bounded flip backend: AMD DC register/sequence adaptations

Pinned source: Linux v6.19.10, commit
271f8eab9590b57a2ff0c8c9eee357723c4a85cb.
https://github.com/gregkh/linux/tree/v6.19.10/drivers/gpu/drm/amd

Adapted subset: arch/x86_64/amd/renoir_registers.h uses numeric offsets/masks
from include/asic_reg/dcn/dcn_2_1_0_offset.h and dcn_2_1_0_sh_mask.h,
include/renoir_ip_offset.h, include/asic_reg/gc/gc_9_0_offset.h,
include/asic_reg/mmhub/mmhub_1_0_offset.h and NBIF direct aliases from
include/asic_reg/nbio/nbio_7_0_offset.h, nbio_7_4_offset.h and
nbio_2_3_offset.h. Firmware table layouts/units come from
include/atomfirmware.h and include/atombios.h.

Local changes: reduced named constants; segment-plus-DWORD offsets converted
to BAR-relative bytes; an original bounded numeric parser and diagnostics.
The flip subset adapts dc/hubp/dcn21/dcn21_hubp.c mono control/high/low ordering,
dc/hubp/dcn10/dcn10_hubp.c completion and pitch/crossbar decoding,
dc/hubp/dcn20/dcn20_hubp.c state/latch ordering, dc/optc/dcn20/dcn20_optc.c
ODM routing, dc/mpc/dcn10/dcn10_mpc.c and dcn20/dcn20_mpc.c route decoding,
dc/dpp/dcn10/dcn10_dpp_dscl.c scaler-bypass decoding and dc/inc/hw/mpc.h enums.
The inherited unity RGB scaler gate additionally reads ratio/phase/tap/control
fields from the same DCN2.1 headers and dcn10_dpp_dscl.c manual mode selection.
No scaler programming is imported or performed.
Local changes: narrow three-register write allowlist, inherited fields retained,
one outstanding request, kernel-owned two-surface state and sleeping completion.
No Linux DRM/BO/VM infrastructure, allocator or ATOM command executor is imported.
No upstream source is downloaded by the build.

The opt-in read-only cursor inventory adds definition subsets from the same
DCN2.1 offset/mask headers: cursor/HUBPREQ, CNVC cursor, per-OPP lock, MPC
pending/taken/ack and OTG update/position fields, plus BASE_IDX1 REFCLK/DP DTO.
Reference-clock candidate arithmetic adapts dc/dccg/dcn20/dcn20_dccg.c and
dc/hubbub/dcn20/dcn20_hubbub.c; the VUPDATE candidate calculation adapts
dc/hwss/dcn10/dcn10_hwseq.c. Numeric ATOM dce_info decoding uses atomfirmware.h
and dc/bios/bios_parser2.c field interpretation. No cursor programming, power
operation, firmware call, latch/retirement predicate or Linux allocator is copied.
dc/dce/dce_clock_source.c is cited research for raw DTO provenance, not imported
clock programming. These diagnostics neither allocate nor map cursor backing.

